    answer: "<p>Yes! We offer 20+ color options for seamless gutters, from classic white and brown to colors that match your trim, fascia, or roof. The color is baked into the aluminum finish, so it won't peel, chip, or fade like painted gutters.</p>"
  - question: How do seamless gutters compare to sectional gutters?
    answer: "<p>Sectional gutters are made from pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together with seams every 10 feet. Each seam is a potential leak point and a place for debris to collect. Seamless gutters are fabricated in one continuous piece (except at corners), eliminating these weak points. While sectional gutters cost less upfront, seamless gutters last longer, leak less, and require less maintenance — making them the better long-term value.</p>"

